  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe optimization task is to find a step function h minimizing the maximum overlap integral C\u2085, subject to h being in [0,1] and its integral being 1. The problem is non-convex and prone to local minima with gradient descent. Our strategy improves upon the parent by:\n\n- Switching from finite difference gradients to exact gradient computation for efficiency.\n- Implementing the Adam optimizer for adaptive learning rates and faster convergence.\n- Maintaining feasibility constraints via clipping and rescaling after each step.\n- Leveraging the provided initial_h_values for a good starting point.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nWe minimize:\n$$ C_5 = \\max_k \\left(1 - \\int_0^2 h(x)h(x+k) dx \\right) $$\nsubject to:\n$$ 0 \\leq h(x) \\leq 1, \\quad \\int_0^2 h(x) dx = 1 $$\n\nThe exact gradient $\\nabla C_5$ for active lag $k$ is computed as:\n$$ \\frac{\\partial C_5}{\\partial h[j]} = (1 - h[j - k])_{\\text{if valid}} - h[j + k]_{\\text{if valid}} $$\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na. Initialize h from initial_h_values or uniform distribution.\nb. Use Adam optimizer with initial learning rate 0.001.\nc. For each iteration:\n   i. Compute cross-correlation and find maximum lag k.\n   ii. Calculate exact gradient for active k.\n   iii. Update h using Adam step.\n   iv. Clip h to [0,1] and rescale to maintain sum constraint.\n   v. Track best solution.\nd. Terminate after budget or when no improvement.\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n- Start with Adam optimizer for better convergence.\n- Use n_points=100 for balance between accuracy and speed.\n- Check feasibility after each step.\n- Consider multiple restarts if time permits.\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\nEach iteration processes exact gradient in O(n_points). With Adam's adaptive steps, convergence is faster than parent.\u4fdd\u5b88 estimate: 10,000 iterations in 600 seconds.\n\n6. Validation and return contract\nEnsure h \u2208 [0,1] and sum(h) = n_points/2. Validate C\u2085 with evaluator. Return best solution found.",
